#
# Lists host-configuration templates shipped beside install-agent-linux.sh in the agent archive.
#
# One line per template: its path relative to this folder, then the placeholders it declares.
# render_host_config (install-agent-linux.sh) replaces each declared #{NAME}# by the value of the
# installer variable NAME, and refuses to install when a placeholder is undeclared, declared but
# unused, or has no value. A line that is exactly #{include:<path>}# inlines another template of
# this list verbatim: that is how the files a root-owned helper writes at run time (Dovecot,
# OpenDKIM, the ACME alias, the local HTTPS vhost, the TeamSpeak unit) live here while the installed
# helper stays byte-identical. Their $name references are expanded by the helper when it runs, not
# by the installer.
#
